@startuml AddOrderSequenceDiagram
title Baker adds an order: add n/... p/... d/... s/... f/... fi/...

actor Baker
participant "BakerCli" as Cli
participant "<<class>>\nParser" as Parser
participant "OrderList" as List
participant "Order" as Order

Baker -> Cli : add n/Alice Tan p/91234567 ...
Cli -> Parser : parseAdd(input)
activate Parser
note right of Parser
  All six fields required.
  Unknown / duplicate / empty
  fields and invalid date or
  phone or size are rejected here,
  before any order is created.
end note
Parser --> Cli : AddOrderDetails
deactivate Parser
create participant ":AddOrderCommand" as Add
Cli -> Add : new AddOrderCommand(details)
Cli -> Add : execute(orders)
Add -> List : generateOrderId()
List --> Add : "O001"
create Order
Add -> Order : new Order(O001, Customer, Cake, dueDate)
Add -> List : add(order)
ref over Add, List : Build confirmation with capacity warning and Customer ID
Add --> Cli : complete confirmation
Cli --> Baker : Added order O001: Alice Tan ...
ref over Cli, List : Save through the callback supplied by Duke
note right of Cli
  On invalid input Parser throws
  CakeQueueException; the CLI
  prints "Error: ..." and no order
  is added (list unchanged).
end note
@enduml
